---
title: Killing a consumer from the web UI (commands through Postgres)
---
sequenceDiagram
    %% Web app: app/routes/workers.py. SQL: app/broker/control.py, app/broker/registry.py.
    %% Worker side: app/worker.py (Worker._command_loop, Worker.kill_consumer).
    %% Workers expose no ports: the web app can only reach them through Postgres.

    participant Browser
    participant App as Web app
    participant DB as Postgres
    box Worker container
        participant W as Worker (command loop)
        participant C as Consumer
    end

    Note over W: At startup the worker registers (heartbeat) and LISTENs on broker_control
    W->>DB: TAKE_COMMANDS
    DB-->>W: none
    W->>W: wait for a notification (at most 1 s)

    Browser->>App: POST /workers/{worker_id}/consumers/{consumer_id}/kill
    App->>DB: SELECT consumer (which message it holds, for the notice)
    DB-->>App: current_message_id
    App->>DB: SEND_COMMAND: INSERT INTO worker_commands (worker_id, 'kill', {consumer_id})

    alt worker is not registered
        DB-->>App: foreign key violation
        App-->>Browser: 303 See Other, notice: worker is not registered anymore
    else worker is registered
        Note right of DB: trigger worker_commands_notify:<br/>pg_notify('broker_control', worker_id)
        DB-->>App: inserted (committed)
        App-->>Browser: 303 See Other, notice: Killed ... while it held message N
        DB-)W: NOTIFY broker_control
        W->>DB: TAKE_COMMANDS: DELETE ... WHERE id IN (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING
        DB-->>W: kill {consumer_id}
        destroy C
        W->>C: task.cancel(): no ack, no nack
        Note over W: The consumer is removed from the worker, so later heartbeats<br/>neither refresh its row nor renew its lease
    end

    loop htmx, every 1 s
        Browser->>App: GET /partials/workers
        App->>DB: list workers and consumers (with heartbeat age)
        DB-->>App: rows
        App-->>Browser: HTML fragment: the consumer shows as lost after 3 s
    end

    Note over DB: The message it held is recovered by the reaper once its lease expires<br/>(see sequence-crash-recovery.mmd)
